  "question": {
    "text": "Consider the family of lines <math><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>μ</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. The equation of a straight line that belongs to both the families is",
    "image": null
  },
