  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>All lines of the family&nbsp;<math><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> are concurrent.</p><p>The point of concurrency is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Similarly, the point of concurrency of lines of&nbsp; the other family is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3,4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo></math> The line of both families is the line passing through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&amp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mn>3,4</mn></mfenced></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo></math>&nbsp;Equation of the required line is <math><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>",
